            <ArticleTitle>Derivation of the Time-Reversal Anomaly for (2+1)-Dimensional Topological Phases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111603</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1103/PhysRevLett.119.111603</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We prove an explicit formula conjectured recently by Wang and Levin for the anomaly of time-reversal symmetry in (2+1)-dimensional fermionic topological quantum field theories. The crucial step is to determine the cross-cap state in terms of the modular S matrix and T^{2} eigenvalues, generalizing the recent analysis by Barkeshli et al. in the bosonic case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
